+## Keys in an ssh-agent
+
+A key no file holds, in a security key, a phone or a Secure Enclave, signs through an
+ssh-agent. Give the client its public key, a `.pub` file, as `--key`: it asks the agent
+at `SSH_AUTH_SOCK` to sign, and writes the signature as `ssh-keygen -Y sign` does
+through that agent. Such a key is `ecdsa-sha2-nistp256` or `ssh-ed25519`.
+
+```sh
+ssh-add -L                                # ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 AAAA… tv@phone
+ssh-add -L | grep tv@phone > phone.pub
+cut -d' ' -f1,2 phone.pub                 # the key as a version or a set names it
+continuum-party --node http://tv:secret@localhost:3000 --key phone.pub \
+  --record tv.record write home/tv/motd '"from the phone"'
+```
+
+Of an ECDSA signature, `s` and the curve's order less `s` both check. The federation
+takes the low one alone, so that nobody makes another event of what the party signed;
+the client makes `s` low, whichever the agent gives.
